I was playing today and realized that something which would be a very hackish
kind of touch is missing from the game.

It seems that me wearing orcish clothes doesn't bother the elves or dwarves, or
vice-versa.  It would be pretty cool if instead, the act of wearing orcish
stuff would send all elves/dwarves in line of sight into a killing frenzy (and
vice versa).  It fits into the mythos, would not be a big change, and is the
sort of thing hack is known for (ala the Hawaiian shirt/shopkeeper thing).

It would also make your low-level character a bit more nervous about putting on
that orcish helm, if he was a lawful type who would otherwise encounter many
peaceful elves and dwarves.

	Alec

BTW, is using poisoned arrows and darts hurt your alignment if you are lawful?
If not, that's another change to consider.



